Resolving the distribution of quantum states requires the partition function for the biomolecules. While this function is not available at the present state of knowledge, for biomolecules with a wide amplitude of structural fluctuations and a large number of low energy conformers, a permissible approximation can be made78. Here, we simplify it by assuming two types of quantum states with those of low energy equally populated and those of higher energy not occupied. Then \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
